    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1307">

                <pb facs="1038" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.77/127.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received, and has
                    communicated to the Secretary of War, your No. 1369, of the 19th instant,
                    transmitting a joint letter from Messrs. T. K. Eccles and J. F. Ealy,
                    representatives, respectively, of the Order of Railway Conductors and the
                    Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers, with relation to some six hundred engineers
                    and conductors who have left the service of the National Railways of Mexico,
                    stating that, should the services of these men be needed by the United States in
                    handling troop trains in the Republic of Mexico, the organizations mentioned
                    would be able to furnish all the men needed, who would be thoroughly familiar
                    with the tracks over which the trains would be run.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
